// =============================================================================
// Sylas, Scout of the Reach — the beat-1 companion first-meeting + recruit (WO-238).
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Canon join order (companion roster): Sylas (beat-1) -> Elara (wave 3) -> Grom
// (first OuterWorld return). This authors the FIRST join as Yarn content so it
// plays through the shared DialogueService runner (tap/click-to-advance, ClassicRPG
// presenter) like every other dialogue, and fires the REAL party-join + quest
// ledger through the command bridges rather than hand-granting.
//
// THE RECRUIT (not hand-granted):
//   <<command: StartQuest companion.sylas>>     -> QuestService ledger (quest opens)
//   <<command: RecruitCompanion Ranger>>        -> GameStateService.AddToParty("Ranger")
//                                                  fires PlayerChanged -> StoryCompanionInjector
//                                                  spawns Sylas's body (follows + fights),
//                                                  PartyHudBridge grows the party frame.
//   <<command: SetQuestFlag companion.sylas met>>-> persisted met-flag
//   <<command: CompleteQuest companion.sylas>>   -> ledger marks the meeting done
// All four verbs are registered in BOTH DialogueCommandBridge (FTUE host) and
// NPCCommandBridge (world-NPC host), so this node works from either launch path.
//
// $sylasMet (declared in _Declarations.yarn) mirrors the ledger flag for cheap
// re-entry branching, the same "stemming" pattern the WO-291 vendor pack uses.
//
// VOICE (narrative bible): Sylas is a grounded woodland scout — wry, watchful,
// economical. The Hollow Ones read as grief, not cartoon villains; no fake-archaic
// speech. He commits to walk WITH the Keeper, on his own terms. ASCII-only.
// =============================================================================
title: SylasFirstMeeting
tags: companion recruit beat1 sylas
---
<<if $sylasMet == true>>
    <<jump SylasGreetAgain>>
<<endif>>

// --- The encounter: he's already had eyes on you ---
Sylas: Hold - easy. Keep your hand off that hilt; if I wanted you down you'd not have heard me at all.
Sylas: I've had eyes on you since the treeline. You're the new Keeper. The Heart's been louder since you came - even out here I felt it stir.

-> Who are you?
    Sylas: Sylas. Scout of the Reach. I've read these woods longer than the Hollow Ones have walked them.
    Sylas: I knew the people who gave themselves to that tree. Some of those Echoes were friends. So I keep the wild off the wall, and I don't ask for thanks.
-> You've been following me.
    Sylas: Watching. There's a difference, and you'll learn it. A scout who follows gets seen. A scout who watches keeps you alive.
    Sylas: I'm Sylas - Scout of the Reach. And I don't trail just anyone through these trees.

// --- The hook: why he matters now ---
Sylas: The wild's been restless. Something past the dark side of this land is pushing them toward Elarion - the Hollow Ones first, and worse behind them.
Sylas: I can read a trail three days cold. You can hold a wall. Apart, we each lose slow. Together, maybe we don't.

// --- The recruit moment: his offer, the player's call ---
-> Then walk with me.
    <<jump SylasAccept>>
-> Why should I trust a stranger in the woods?
    Sylas: You shouldn't. Not on my word. So trust the arrow - I'll put one in whatever finds us first, and you can decide what I'm worth after.
    -> ...Fair. Walk with me, Sylas.
        <<jump SylasAccept>>
    -> I work alone.
        <<jump SylasDecline>>
===

title: SylasAccept
tags: companion recruit sylas
---
// Open the meeting quest in the real ledger, JOIN the party (spawns his body +
// grows the party frame), persist the met-flag, then close the quest. Sylas is the
// Ranger companion by canon; if the player themselves chose Ranger, the standalone
// SylasFirstMeeting.cs beat handles the different-class substitution - this Yarn
// path is the explicit, story-first recruit and names the Ranger directly.
<<command: StartQuest companion.sylas>>
<<command: RecruitCompanion Ranger>>
<<command: SetQuestFlag companion.sylas met>>
<<set $sylasMet to true>>

Sylas: <i>He lowers the bow, and something in his shoulders eases.</i> Then it's settled. I walk where you walk, Keeper - and I put an arrow in whatever finds us first.
Sylas: Stay near the wall when the horns sound. Out here, I'll go first - I always have.
Sylas: Lead on. Let's see what the dark side of this land is hiding.

<<command: CompleteQuest companion.sylas>>
===

title: SylasDecline
tags: companion sylas
---
// He doesn't join now, but the door stays open - the standalone beat / a later
// approach can re-offer. We deliberately do NOT set $sylasMet, so the recruit can
// still fire on a later meeting.
Sylas: Suit yourself. Proud gets you killed out here, but it's your wall to bleed for.
Sylas: <i>He fades back toward the trees.</i> I'll be in the treeline when you change your mind, Keeper. You will.
===

title: SylasGreetAgain
tags: companion ambient sylas
---
// Re-entry once Sylas has already joined (mirrors the vendor "bonded" branch).
Sylas: Still breathing, Keeper. Good. The treeline's quiet - for now. Say the word and I'll scout ahead.
===
